# ── Raw source archive ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your original per-project folders ("1 Makan Mania", "2 Astro Cow", ...)
# hold screenshots, videos, installers and Visual Studio source. Two of the
# videos are over GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, which makes a push
# fail outright, and git keeps every blob in history forever — so one
# accidental commit bloats the repo permanently.
#
# Matched by the leading digit in their names. The web assets live in
# assets/img/<slug>/ (magique/, astro-cow/, ...) and ARE tracked.
assets/img/[0-9]*/

# Old flat layout. Every web asset now lives in assets/img/<slug>/, so
# nothing loose at the top of assets/img/ should be tracked (the fetch
# script is the one exception, and it has no image extension).
# The stale files are still on your disk — safe to delete by hand.
assets/img/*.png
assets/img/*.jpg
assets/img/*.jpeg
assets/img_old/

# Media that belongs on YouTube or itch, not in git
*.mov
*.exe
*.msi

# Source GIFs — the web copies are assets/img/<slug>/cover.mp4 + .webm
assets/img/*/*.gif

# Build noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
